// lib-wazuh-active-response (C9 v0): the guardrails that need the Wazuh API,
// after "Plan": the agent is listed by n8n-response (so it is in
// response.agent_group) and active; the address isn't any agent's
// (protect_agent_ips: every agent n8n-api lists, ip and registerIP); and for
// a live send, the rate cap (live sends in the last hour, all alerts
// together: this workflow's static data, written by "Result"). Reached by one
// path: the lookups done, or the first one that failed. A failed lookup is
// `not_sent` (nothing was sent; fail closed), a guardrail `refused`.
// Addresses: IPv4 and IPv6 (an embedded IPv4 tail allowed), as BigInt; an
// IPv4-mapped IPv6 address (::ffff:a.b.c.d) is checked as IPv4. Pure.
